\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \ulc0 Version 6.3.7 (2026/04/10)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - Added a new option in the "Websites" settings for the default URL scheme (http or https), which is used to autocomplete incompletely entered URLs \
- A new \'84URL mapping\'93 feature (accessible via the "Tools" menu) has been added. This feature allows you to modify URLs according to your own rules before the respective webpage loads. Using this feature, you can redirect certain webpages to others, filter tracking parameters from the URLs, open alternative webpages, and much more. The feature comes with a set of predefined rules, but you can also define your own custom rules. \
\pard\tx593\pardeftab593\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The following predefined rules are provided:\
  * YouTube Embedded Player: These rules allow users to switch YouTube video pages to the "embedded" version, which contains only the video; there are no comments, no suggestions, and (currently) no ads.\
  * YouTube Shorts: This rule automatically redirects YouTube Shorts to the regular video page, so they load in the full video player instead of the stripped-down Shorts player. \
  * Reddit: Redirects to the old/classic Reddit layout\
  * Tracking: Various rules for removing tracking parameters from URLs\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Note: The \'84URL mapping" feature should be used with caution, as websites aren't designed to handle it and may not always work properly. However, it can certainly help you avoid some of the web's annoyances.\
- A new option is available in the context menu for links: "Download (Save in\'85)\'93 allows you to select the destination folder where the download should be saved (as an alternative to the default download folder)\
- Several visual changes have been made for macOS 26/Liquid Glass\
- Pocket has been removed as an option for the reading list because the Pocket service has been discontinued\
- Bug fix: When loading ZIP-based web archives from older versions of iCab, an additional empty window might have opened\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
\
Version 6.3.6 (2025/11/16)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - Because of a bug in Apples new macOS 26 Frameworks, loading web archive files did no longer work. A new workaround should solve this issue again.\
\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
Version 6.3.5 (2025/11/07)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - The reading list can now also be accessed via an icon in the toolbar if desired\
- The OpenURL AppleScript command now also supports a \'93file\'94 URL (as the target path where the file is saved) for the \'93to\'94 parameter, as an alternative to the pure file name (where the file would end up in the Downloads folder under the given name)\
- When opening windows (when activating the app, when receiving a URL from other apps, when launching the App), the \'93Prefer private windows\'94 setting is now evaluated.\
- There is now also a file browser so that entire folders dragged from the Finder into the app can be viewed in the browser window. However, system folders and protected folders are excluded.\
- There is a new module that allows you to redirect videos from YouTube video pages to the YouTube embedded player. This hides everything except the video itself (i.e., comments, suggestions, chats, etc. are hidden. Currently, all advertising is also blocked).\
- There are new additional values for the \'93toWindow\'94 parameter of the \'93OpenURL\'94 AppleScript command. The following values are now available:\
  >0: Open in existing tab/window with this index\
    0: New window (the \'93private\'94 status is determined by the \'93Prefer private windows/tabs\'94 setting)\
   -1: Open in active tab/window (the \'93private\'94 status of the tab/window remains unchanged)\
   -2: New tab (the \'93private\'94 status is determined by the \'93Prefer private windows/tabs\'94 setting)\
   -3: Open in a new private window\
   -4: Open in a new private tab\
   -5: Open in a new non-private window\
   -6: Open in a new non-private tab\
\
- Due to a bug in the Mac version of Safari, Safari was unable to import exported bookmarks. A workaround in iCab now ensures that Safari can read the bookmarks again despite this bug.\
\
- Bugfix: Some modules without their own module settings could not be accessed.\
- Bugfix: Closing a window with protected tabs could lead to a \'93dead\'94 window.\
- Bugfix: AppleScript should now also open new windows privately when the \'93Prefer Private Tabs\'94 option is active.\
- Bugfix: Windows without tabs were not saved in the tabs session and could therefore not be restored the next time the app was launched.\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
\
Version 6.3.4 (2025/06/17)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - Bugfix: The Workaround for the bug within the Apple developer tools still had an unwanted side effect.\
\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
Version 6.3.3 (2025/06/17)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - The latest macOS developer tools from Apple have a serious bug which can create broken code for some Intel Macs and macOS releases. This resulted in crashes on certain Intel-Mac and macOS releases. Not affected by this bug were Intel Macs with macOS 10.x or Sequoia, and Apple-Silicon Macs. This new update contains a workaround which avoids the crash \
\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
Version 6.3.2 (2025/06/07)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - Spanish Translation added, many thanks to Samir G\'e4rtner who translated the App\
- It\'92s now possible to export and import cookies (all or only the selected ones) from within the \'84Web Storage\'93 window. This feature uses the Netscape Cookies file format and therefore allows to exchange cookies with other browsers supporting the same file format\
- WebAuthn is now supported\
- Bugfix: If a web site in a background tab tried to print itself, the App froze\
- Bugfix: If a web site provided an extremely long file name for a download (> 255 characters), the file could not be saved.\
- Bugfix: In Kiosk mode the favorites toolbar was not shown even if it was explicitly enabled for the Kiosk.\
\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
Version 6.3.1 (2025/03/07)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - A bug in macOS 11.x could cause a crash (Apple fixed it with macOS 12). The new iCab update  includes a workaround for this macOS bug, so the App will work under macOS 11 as well\
- The Bookmarks import feature now also supports importing the \'84Quickstarter\'93 of iCab Mobile (iPhone, iPad)\
- Adds a few accessibility labels in the sidebar for VoiceOver users.\
\

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \
Version 6.3 (2025/02/17)\
\

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \ulnone - New highlighter feature: If you open the context menu (right-click, control-click) for the selected text on a web page, you can now highlight this text in color or remove the respective color again. The color markings are permanently retained (as long as the page does not change significantly). Via the menu \'93Tools > Website tools > Highlighters\'94, all pages with highlighters are listed and you can also delete these here if these are no longer required.\
- New auto-click feature: If you open the context menu (right-click, control-click) over a page element (link, button), you can use the \'93Auto-click element\'94 option to select a page element that is automatically clicked every time the page is opened. This can be particularly useful for cookie banners to close them automatically via a specific button. All pages on which an element is automatically clicked are listed via the \'93Tools > Website tools > Auto-click\'94 menu. Here you can also delete entries that are not longer needed. Auto-click works as long as the website does not change significantly.\
- New element hiding feature: If you open the context menu (right-click, control-click) on a page element and select the \'93Hide elements\'94 item from the menu, page elements around the clicked item can be hidden. This can be useful to hide unwanted page elements and works as long as the web page does not change significantly. However, only paragraphs/broader sections can be hidden. The area to be hidden can be increased or decreased via a small window using \'93+\'94/\'93-\'94 buttons and applied to the entire domains or the specific page only. Important: If elements (such as advertising) can be blocked using normal filters, you should also use filters.\
- The \'93Universal Links\'94 feature of macOS can be deactivated. Universal links allow other apps to redirect links to their own web service to themselves. This means that an Amazon app could redirect all Amazon links that are clicked in the browser to itself. If you do not want this, you can now disable it in the \'93Web Sites\'94 settings.\
- Support for the HandOff feature of macOS (transferring a session between Mac/iOS devices) now supports not only iCab and iCab Mobile, but also other browsers (the URL of the current window/tab only). \
- Pasting a URL into the Downloads window will immediately create a new download for this URL\
- Bugfix: If you tried to save a page with a page title longer than 200 characters, the app could crash \

