- The new "
\f0\b TopTen
\f1\b0 " feature will open an overview (similar to Expos\'e9) with thumbnails of the most visited, last visited or the favorites pages. The TopTen feature can be opened from within the Navigation menu or with the button to the left of the Favorites button. The button in the Favorites button can be switched off in the experimental settings. The very first time the TopTen feature is opened, it can take a while to load all the thumbnails. Later they will open much faster because the thumbnails are cached and reused. iCab needs to count the number of times you open certain web pages for the "most visited" pages, and it needs some time to get accurate counter values. You can remove pages from the list by clicking the "X". A green star will be attached to web pages where the server sends the modification date, to indicate that this page was modified within the last 24 hours. But be aware that many modern web pages like blogs and news sites are modified multiple times a day, so this modification information is not very useful for these sites.\
\
- Now, iCab adds the text encoding information of the web page into the meta-data of the file when a web page is saved as HTML or text file.\
