\
- It's now possible to add tags for bookmark folders as well.\
\
- New setting in the Preferences dialog (JavaScript settings) and in the Filter Manager (also in the JavaScript settings) added to allow/disallow JavaScript to process Cmd-Clicks. Some Web pages process Cmd-Clicks themselves and therefore do prevent that the user can open links in a new window or Tab (which is done by clicking a link while the Cmd key is pressed), so when JavaScript is no longer allowed to process Cmd-Clicks, the user will be always able to open links in new windows or Tabs. In general these web sites which process Cmd-Clicks do not really need to process Cmd clicks, they are almost always programmed so that they try to capture all modifier keys (Cmd, Shift, Control, Alt) which are available and do the same thing for all of these modifier keys. So blocking the Cmd-Key should not harm any web page.\
\
- The triangle that marks a folder in the Favorites toolbar can be switched off in the experimental settings.\
